@startuml hunger-priority-communication
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FEF9C3
skinparam noteBorderColor #CA8A04
skinparam participantBorderColor #334155
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9

title Hunger / Priority Peer-to-Peer Communication & Priority Scheduling

participant "PhilosopherAgent\n(Philosopher-2: Aristotle)" as P2 #EFF6FF
participant "PhilosopherAgent\n(Philosopher-1: Plato)" as P1 #EFF6FF
participant "EnvironmentAgent\n(Resource Authority)" as Env #F0FDF4

autonumber

== 1. Dynamic Hunger Accumulation & Priority Trigger ==
note over P2
  Aristotle waiting/thinking.
  Hunger reaches **78 >= 75** (HIGH Priority).
  Triggers **checkAndBroadcastPriority()**.
end note

== 2. Peer-to-Peer ACL Priority Broadcast ==
P2 -> P1 : **ACL: INFORM**\nconv-id: "hunger-priority"\ncontent: ""HUNGER_PRIORITY:id=2:name=Aristotle:hunger=78:priority=HIGH""
activate P1

note over P1
  Receives message via
  **MessageTemplate.MatchConversationId("hunger-priority")**.
  Registers Aristotle's high priority.
end note

P1 --> P2 : **ACL: INFORM (Reply)**\nconv-id: "hunger-priority"\ncontent: ""PRIORITY_ACK:id=1:name=Plato""
deactivate P1

== 3. Contention for Shared Resource (Fork 2) ==
note over Env
  Fork 2 is currently **occupied** (e.g., held by Socrates).
end note

P1 -> Env : **ACL: REQUEST**\nconv-id: "dining-philosophers"\nreply-with: "req-p1-f2"\ncontent: ""FORK_REQUEST:2""
activate Env
Env --> P1 : **ACL: INFORM**\nin-reply-to: "req-p1-f2"\ncontent: ""WAIT:2""\n[Enqueued in forkQueues[2], Hunger=32]
deactivate Env

P2 -> Env : **ACL: REQUEST**\nconv-id: "dining-philosophers"\nreply-with: "req-p2-f2"\ncontent: ""FORK_REQUEST:2""
activate Env
Env --> P2 : **ACL: INFORM**\nin-reply-to: "req-p2-f2"\ncontent: ""WAIT:2""\n[Enqueued in forkQueues[2], Hunger=78]
deactivate Env

== 4. Environment Priority Resolution with Aging ==
note over Env
  Holder releases Fork 2 (""RELEASE_FORK"").
  Environment invokes **selectBestWaitingRequest(forkQueues[2])**:
  
  **Effective Priority Formula:**
  ""effectivePriority = initialHunger + (waitSeconds * 8.0)""
  
  - Aristotle (P2): ""78 + (1.2 * 8.0) = 87.6""  -> **HIGHEST**
  - Plato (P1):     ""32 + (2.5 * 8.0) = 52.0""
end note

Env --> P2 : **ACL: AGREE**\nconv-id: "dining-philosophers"\nin-reply-to: "req-p2-f2"\ncontent: ""FORK_GRANTED:2""
activate P2
note over P2
  Aristotle receives Fork 2 first
  due to high priority!
end note
deactivate P2

note over P1
  **Starvation Prevention Guarantee:**
  Plato's effective priority continues increasing (+8.0/sec).
  Plato will be served next once Fork 2 is released.
end note

@enduml
